&Q000766

{1 = 1-10}
1.	The Tamarisk opened his mouth and spoke. 
2.	He addressed the Date Palm: 
3.	@q[Tamarisk,Date Palm]{“My body … 
4.	… the bodies of the gods. 
5.	@noteref{The reference is to statues of tamarisk wood.} You grow your fruits but someone places  
6.	them before me like a maid approaching her mistress. 
7.	You do not provide the measuring vessels. 
8.	You are …… minor crops, 
9.	but I ……. 
10.	Your attendants …… before me for you.”} 

{11 = 11-19}
11.	In his anger the Date Palm answered him. 
12.	He addressed his brother the Tamarisk: 
13.	@q[Date Palm,Tamarisk]{“You say: 
14.	@q[Tamarisk,Date Palm]{“If people build daises for me and beautify them too, 
15.	they certainly do not swear by the gods before clay (?).”} 
16.	-- You may be the body of the gods in their shrines and people may name with a good name the daises of the gods, 
17.	but it is silver that can pride itself as the overlay of the gods. 
18.	……, 
19.	describe your beauty!”} @gap{unknown no. of lines missing} 
